1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:04,352
Welcome, everyone, to today's special meeting on biblical prophecy.

2
00:00:04,864 --> 00:00:10,752
Our gathering today has a title, and the title is "At the Appointed Time."

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,288
You might ask,

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,080
who could be so purposeful,

5
00:00:14,336 --> 00:00:15,616
so thoughtful and deliberate,

6
00:00:16,384 --> 00:00:17,664
as to work by an appointed time?

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,712
And what exactly is it all meant to accomplish?

8
00:00:19,712 --> 00:00:23,000
Well, in just a little while, it will all become clear to us.

9
00:00:24,576 --> 00:00:29,696
In the recent war between Russia and Ukraine, I once saw a scene like this.

10
00:00:29,952 --> 00:00:36,096
Someone had laid out a great many toys, right there along the border of Romania and

11
00:00:36,352 --> 00:00:37,376
Ukraine.

12
00:00:37,632 --> 00:00:38,400
What they were doing

13
00:00:38,656 --> 00:00:43,264
was making sure that the children fleeing the war could each receive a toy of their own.

14
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,360
It made me think of the saying: the flames of war are merciless,

15
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:49,408
yet here in this world there is still love.

16
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:52,736
And in fact, human beings are made in the very image of God.

17
00:00:53,504 --> 00:00:55,296
The Bible tells us that God is love.

18
00:00:55,552 --> 00:00:58,112
And my hope is that, through today's gathering,

19
00:00:58,368 --> 00:00:59,648
everyone here would come to know God,

20
00:00:59,648 --> 00:01:01,447
and to come to know His love.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,280
The Chinese people are very clever,

22
00:01:06,048 --> 00:01:07,072
and the Chinese characters

23
00:01:08,096 --> 00:01:09,120
are full of meaning.

24
00:01:09,632 --> 00:01:12,192
Take the character for "God" — it actually has two parts to it.

25
00:01:12,704 --> 00:01:15,264
On one side is the radical 示, the "spirit" or "altar" radical,

26
00:01:16,032 --> 00:01:17,824
and on the other side is the character 申.

27
00:01:19,104 --> 00:01:20,640
Now the ancient form of 示 —

28
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,456
if you look at the image here, you'll see that

29
00:01:23,712 --> 00:01:25,760
the single top stroke represents the firmament, the sky above,

30
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:28,832
the two strokes represent what lies above the firmament,

31
00:01:29,344 --> 00:01:34,464
and the three vertical strokes represent what shines down from the heavens —

32
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,744
the light of the sun, the moon, and the stars.

33
00:01:36,768 --> 00:01:37,792
And so,

34
00:01:38,048 --> 00:01:41,632
the people of old felt that the heavens display their signs,

35
00:01:41,888 --> 00:01:43,680
and from that they could perceive

36
00:01:43,936 --> 00:01:45,216
the very meaning of Heaven.

37
00:01:45,984 --> 00:01:51,360
And the character 申, in its ancient form, carries the sense of a pair of hands reaching out,

38
00:01:51,872 --> 00:01:53,408
a pair of outstretched arms.

39
00:01:56,224 --> 00:01:59,296
So how does the Bible itself describe God

40
00:01:59,552 --> 00:02:03,648
making this firmament? It records it like this — what does it say?

41
00:02:03,904 --> 00:02:04,928
God said,

42
00:02:05,696 --> 00:02:07,232
"Let there be lights in the firmament of the heavens

43
00:02:07,744 --> 00:02:09,024
to divide the day from the night;

44
00:02:09,536 --> 00:02:10,304
and let them be for signs

45
00:02:10,816 --> 00:02:11,840
and for seasons,

46
00:02:12,096 --> 00:02:12,864
and for days

47
00:02:13,632 --> 00:02:14,400
and for years;

48
00:02:15,424 --> 00:02:16,960
and let them be for lights in the firmament of the heavens

49
00:02:17,472 --> 00:02:19,008
to give light upon the earth";

50
00:02:19,776 --> 00:02:21,312
and it was so.

51
00:02:22,336 --> 00:02:24,128
Then God made two great lights:

52
00:02:24,384 --> 00:02:26,432
the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night.

53
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:27,968
He made the stars also.

54
00:02:28,992 --> 00:02:30,272
God set these lights

55
00:02:30,528 --> 00:02:31,552
in the firmament of the heavens

56
00:02:31,808 --> 00:02:32,832
to give light upon the earth,

57
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,648
to rule over the day and the night, and to divide the light from the darkness.

58
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:37,184
And God saw

59
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,208
that it was good.

60
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:42,816
I wonder whether you noticed —

61
00:02:43,072 --> 00:02:46,912
even in that short little passage, you can already come to know God.

62
00:02:47,424 --> 00:02:50,496
Just think about how God made the lights of heaven. It says, "God said" —

63
00:02:51,008 --> 00:02:52,032
that is, God simply spoke,

64
00:02:52,032 --> 00:02:54,526
and then it says, "and it was so."

65
00:02:54,848 --> 00:02:56,384
It turns out that God is full of mighty power:

66
00:02:56,896 --> 00:02:58,432
the very things He speaks simply come to pass.

67
00:02:58,432 --> 00:03:01,760
So in English there's actually a word for this —

68
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,064
the word for the cosmos, "universe."

69
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:07,648
"Universe" — "uni," or "uno," means one,

70
00:03:07,648 --> 00:03:10,000
and "verse" means a single utterance, a word.

71
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,160
People held a concept of where the universe came from:

72
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,160
it came from one word of God, simply spoken into being.

73
00:03:16,608 --> 00:03:20,448
And notice, too, at the very end — "and God saw that it was good."

74
00:03:20,448 --> 00:03:22,680
I think God has a wonderful sense of leisure;

75
00:03:22,752 --> 00:03:24,800
He isn't only ever busy at work.

76
00:03:25,056 --> 00:03:27,872
He is also able to stop and take delight in what He has made.

77
00:03:28,128 --> 00:03:29,920
Today, God is the very One who made you,

78
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:31,456
He understands you best of all,

79
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:33,248
and He is the One most able to take delight in you.

80
00:03:35,296 --> 00:03:36,320
Let me ask you all a question.

81
00:03:37,856 --> 00:03:40,672
Which do you think is bigger — the moon, or the sun?

82
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,920
You might think

83
00:03:42,976 --> 00:03:44,768
this question is really far too silly —

84
00:03:44,768 --> 00:03:47,003
of course the sun is the bigger one.

85
00:03:47,328 --> 00:03:48,352
But the people of old,

86
00:03:48,864 --> 00:03:53,472
some of them would say the moon is bigger. And why? Because sometimes, on a dark night, when you

87
00:03:53,728 --> 00:03:59,872
look up at the moon, it looks enormous — have you ever heard of the "supermoon"?

88
00:04:00,128 --> 00:04:04,640
Or when you climb up a mountain and see the moon smiling down at you,

89
00:04:04,736 --> 00:04:09,856
that is what we call the "moon illusion."

90
00:04:10,624 --> 00:04:13,696
And still others had an explanation like this. What did they say?

91
00:04:13,952 --> 00:04:16,512
When you look up and the moon appears so large,

92
00:04:16,768 --> 00:04:20,040
and the sun also appears about that large — when the two seem about the same size,

93
00:04:20,095 --> 00:04:21,375
and yet the sun is so very hot

94
00:04:21,631 --> 00:04:24,191
and the moon so very cold — just think, if you were

95
00:04:24,703 --> 00:04:25,983
sitting beside a stove,

96
00:04:26,239 --> 00:04:29,311
the closer you are the hotter it is, and the farther away the colder, right?

97
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:32,895
So that would mean the moon is the one near to us, and the sun is the one far off —

98
00:04:33,151 --> 00:04:34,687
but since the two appear about the same size,

99
00:04:34,943 --> 00:04:38,783
if the moon is farther and still looks that big, that would prove the moon is the bigger one.

100
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:41,343
So in the old days, people would actually argue it like that.

101
00:04:41,855 --> 00:04:45,695
But that passage from a moment ago — the Bible has already given me the answer.

102
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,767
God made the two great lights, the greater to rule the day.

103
00:04:49,791 --> 00:04:55,167
In the daytime, when the sun is out, most of the time you can't even see the moon — the greater rules the day, the lesser rules the night.

104
00:04:55,423 --> 00:04:57,727
Already, over three thousand years ago,

105
00:04:57,983 --> 00:05:00,000
this one passage of Scripture had already told

106
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:03,615
me that the sun is, in fact, bigger than the moon.

107
00:05:04,639 --> 00:05:07,455
And moonlight is something very special.

108
00:05:07,711 --> 00:05:12,319
Its glow is bright and pure, and when the moon is full it is very large indeed.

109
00:05:12,831 --> 00:05:13,855
I think it really is beautiful —

110
00:05:14,111 --> 00:05:15,647
like a great big street-lamp.

111
00:05:16,415 --> 00:05:22,047
Isn't moonlight romantic? And yet you needn't ever worry about bumping into a lamppost.

112
00:05:22,047 --> 00:05:24,338
Now if you look up high,

113
00:05:24,351 --> 00:05:25,375
apart from the sun,

114
00:05:25,631 --> 00:05:26,143
and apart from

115
00:05:26,655 --> 00:05:27,679
the full moon,

116
00:05:28,191 --> 00:05:30,495
what is the third brightest thing up there?

117
00:05:30,751 --> 00:05:32,287
It isn't Sirius,

118
00:05:32,543 --> 00:05:36,383
and it isn't the North Star either — most of the time, it is the planet Venus.

119
00:05:36,639 --> 00:05:42,783
This is what many people call the morning star: just before daybreak, you can see

120
00:05:43,039 --> 00:05:44,831
one single, especially bright star.

121
00:05:45,087 --> 00:05:49,183
When you see the morning star, daybreak is very near, and the sun is about to rise.

122
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:52,255
And so, within the Bible,

123
00:05:52,511 --> 00:05:53,791
through this morning star,

124
00:05:54,303 --> 00:05:58,399
God reminds us and teaches us something. Here is what it says:

125
00:05:58,911 --> 00:06:01,471
It says: we also have the prophetic word made more sure,

126
00:06:01,727 --> 00:06:03,007
like a lamp shining in a dark place,

127
00:06:04,543 --> 00:06:09,919
which you do well to heed, until the day dawns and the morning star rises in your hearts.

128
00:06:10,175 --> 00:06:12,223
The Bible uses the morning star

129
00:06:12,735 --> 00:06:14,015
to speak of prophecy —

130
00:06:14,527 --> 00:06:16,575
as if, together in the darkness,

131
00:06:17,599 --> 00:06:21,695
when you have no direction and no hope, you catch sight of the morning star,

132
00:06:21,951 --> 00:06:28,095
and you know daybreak is near. In the same way, prophecy lets me know that the words of the Bible are true.

133
00:06:28,607 --> 00:06:30,143
God's promises are true.

134
00:06:31,167 --> 00:06:33,471
So many circumstances, so many troubles, will one day pass away,

135
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:35,263
and God will bring hope.

136
00:06:35,519 --> 00:06:40,639
Speaking of prophecy, let me mention in passing — some of the Bible's prophecies have not yet happened,

137
00:06:40,895 --> 00:06:42,431
some are being fulfilled right now,

138
00:06:42,687 --> 00:06:45,247
but far more of them have already come to pass.

139
00:06:45,759 --> 00:06:51,903
So the Bible has a saying: declare the former things, what they were — that is, to make clear

140
00:06:52,159 --> 00:06:54,463
what has happened, and how it came about,

141
00:06:54,975 --> 00:06:57,279
so that we would know that the Bible,

142
00:06:57,535 --> 00:07:03,679
the word of God, is so accurate and so remarkable. And tonight's gathering is for exactly that purpose.

143
00:07:05,471 --> 00:07:10,847
And then, at the very end of the Bible, the Lord Jesus Himself says: I am the bright morning star.

144
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:15,120
Look back at this world — think of how severe the pandemic has been,

145
00:07:16,991 --> 00:07:18,271
and Europe once again at war.

146
00:07:18,271 --> 00:07:20,813
What on earth will become of the world that lies ahead?

147
00:07:20,813 --> 00:07:21,855
But I find this so precious:

148
00:07:21,855 --> 00:07:23,647
the Lord says that He is the bright morning star.

149
00:07:23,903 --> 00:07:25,183
He is the One who brings hope to people.

150
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:32,095
And you'll notice, too, that when God made the lights of heaven —

151
00:07:32,607 --> 00:07:33,119
wow —

152
00:07:33,375 --> 00:07:35,935
there was the sun, there was the moon, and there were all the stars.

153
00:07:36,959 --> 00:07:39,263
And what were they for? They were to give light in the sky,

154
00:07:39,519 --> 00:07:45,663
and to shine upon the earth. And this phrase is mentioned twice — "to shine upon the earth" — to let you know that all God made

155
00:07:45,919 --> 00:07:47,199
was, in fact, for you.

156
00:07:48,735 --> 00:07:50,783
Such enormous heavenly bodies, all brought into being,

157
00:07:51,039 --> 00:07:51,807
were made for your sake.

158
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:53,599
So great a moon,

159
00:07:53,855 --> 00:07:58,207
so great a sun brought forth — it was for you, to give its light upon the earth.

160
00:07:58,463 --> 00:07:59,743
Doesn't it shine its light down upon you?

161
00:08:01,023 --> 00:08:05,119
These lights have a real purpose: to divide the day from the night,

162
00:08:05,375 --> 00:08:08,191
and to be for signs, for seasons, for days, and for years.

163
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:12,287
So God taught — that is, through the very things He made, He taught the people of Israel

164
00:08:12,543 --> 00:08:13,055
a great many things.

165
00:08:13,567 --> 00:08:15,615
And the very first of them is this: how is a single day reckoned?

166
00:08:16,127 --> 00:08:16,895
It is that first there was

167
00:08:18,175 --> 00:08:18,943
the evening,

168
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,735
and then the morning — and that is counted as one day.

169
00:08:20,991 --> 00:08:24,063
So how does a Jewish day actually begin? It begins

170
00:08:24,319 --> 00:08:30,463
from the sunset of one day, at dusk, and runs all the way to the dusk of the next day.

171
00:08:30,719 --> 00:08:34,815
And in this you can see that God greatly desires that people would have rest.

172
00:08:37,375 --> 00:08:41,983
And then there is that word for "appointed season" — it is a very special word indeed.

173
00:08:42,239 --> 00:08:47,359
You'll find some Bibles translate it as "seasons," but many others translate it as "festivals,"

174
00:08:47,615 --> 00:08:49,151
or even as "special meetings."

175
00:08:49,407 --> 00:08:51,455
It turns out that the word for "appointed season" —

176
00:08:51,711 --> 00:08:57,087
its original meaning, the sense of the original language, is this: an appointed date,

177
00:08:57,343 --> 00:08:58,879
an agreed-upon time.

178
00:08:59,647 --> 00:09:03,743
So to translate it as "festival" is very meaningful too — it means that God

179
00:09:04,511 --> 00:09:05,279
appoints a time with people and calls them to keep the feast,

180
00:09:07,071 --> 00:09:11,935
appoints a time so that people would return before Him and enjoy that shared joy together.

181
00:09:12,447 --> 00:09:12,959
That is what it truly means.

182
00:09:14,239 --> 00:09:15,519
And so, within the Bible,

183
00:09:15,775 --> 00:09:18,847
God taught the people of Israel just how to keep the feasts.

184
00:09:20,895 --> 00:09:26,527
And one of them is this — the very first thing mentioned when God teaches people to keep a feast is the Sabbath.

185
00:09:27,039 --> 00:09:31,391
And what does the Sabbath mean? It means that for six days there is work you ought to do,

186
00:09:32,159 --> 00:09:32,927
but on the seventh day,

187
00:09:33,183 --> 00:09:34,463
you lay down the work of your hands

188
00:09:34,719 --> 00:09:36,255
and you come to rest.

189
00:09:36,255 --> 00:09:39,240
So you can see that God

190
00:09:39,583 --> 00:09:41,631
first gave people the evening and then the morning,

191
00:09:41,887 --> 00:09:42,655
six days

192
00:09:43,423 --> 00:09:48,543
of labor, and then rest on the seventh. From this you can see that God truly calls people

193
00:09:48,799 --> 00:09:50,335
to have real enjoyment,

194
00:09:50,335 --> 00:09:52,280
that God truly calls people to enjoy their rest.

195
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:58,200
When the Lord Jesus came, He too said this — He spoke of Himself in particular as the Lord of the Sabbath.

196
00:09:58,271 --> 00:10:01,855
And what did He say? "Come to Me, all you who labor and are heavy laden,

197
00:10:02,111 --> 00:10:03,391
come to Me,

198
00:10:03,903 --> 00:10:05,695
and I will give you rest."

199
00:10:06,975 --> 00:10:08,255
I wonder, in your own life,

200
00:10:08,511 --> 00:10:13,375
in all that you have been through, whether you ever feel that life lays so many burdens upon you,

201
00:10:13,887 --> 00:10:14,911
that you are carrying a heavy load.

202
00:10:14,911 --> 00:10:17,600
In fact, when the Lord Jesus came, He is well able to understand you.

203
00:10:17,727 --> 00:10:21,311
He is able to sympathize with you, and He longs for you to set down your heavy burden.

204
00:10:21,567 --> 00:10:22,847
He longs for you to come and rest.

205
00:10:22,847 --> 00:10:24,694
This is the very heart of God.

206
00:10:26,687 --> 00:10:28,223
So God called the people of Israel

207
00:10:28,223 --> 00:10:30,223
to keep the feasts —

208
00:10:30,271 --> 00:10:31,807
and there are seven feasts in all.

209
00:10:31,807 --> 00:10:35,237
We call them the Feasts of the LORD.

210
00:10:35,903 --> 00:10:38,207
And you'll find something fascinating about these seven feasts:

211
00:10:39,231 --> 00:10:43,327
they seem to cluster at two times — you could call them the autumn feasts

212
00:10:43,839 --> 00:10:45,119
and the spring feasts.

213
00:10:46,655 --> 00:10:48,959
Let me think — now that I'm here in America,

214
00:10:49,471 --> 00:10:55,615
in many places, much of the time, there's a holiday every single month —

215
00:10:55,871 --> 00:10:57,407
every month there's a so-called long weekend.

216
00:10:57,407 --> 00:11:00,054
Having a holiday every month is nice, but you'll notice

217
00:11:01,247 --> 00:11:05,343
something fascinating: these seven feasts are not scattered evenly across every month.

218
00:11:05,343 --> 00:11:09,320
And you'll see there are three of them marked in red.

219
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,719
The Sabbath

220
00:11:10,975 --> 00:11:17,119
is when you rest at home, laying down all your work, to be at rest; but keeping these feasts was something different.

221
00:11:17,375 --> 00:11:18,911
Three times a year,

222
00:11:19,167 --> 00:11:22,495
the people of Israel were to go up to Jerusalem to keep the feast there,

223
00:11:23,007 --> 00:11:23,775
to go up to the temple

224
00:11:24,031 --> 00:11:25,311
and worship God in that place.

225
00:11:25,311 --> 00:11:30,175
And here is something fascinating too — God called them up to Jerusalem,

226
00:11:30,175 --> 00:11:33,247
and you'll see that all of these feasts fall in the dry season.

227
00:11:33,503 --> 00:11:38,623
Not in the rainy season — for if they had to go up to Jerusalem, traveling far, and the rains came,

228
00:11:38,623 --> 00:11:43,743
everywhere would be mud and mire.

229
00:11:43,743 --> 00:11:44,767
But you'll find that God, for their sake,

230
00:11:45,023 --> 00:11:46,303
so that they could keep the feast,

231
00:11:46,303 --> 00:11:48,103
so that they could walk out His word —

232
00:11:48,351 --> 00:11:49,631
you'll find that there was a dry season,

233
00:11:49,887 --> 00:11:52,191
and God's promise too: when they went up,

234
00:11:53,215 --> 00:11:59,359
no one would seize their fields or take their property. On the contrary, when the people of Israel

235
00:11:59,359 --> 00:12:01,466
kept the feast in this way, the whole land was at peace on every side.

236
00:12:03,711 --> 00:12:05,247
But in fact, within the Bible

237
00:12:05,759 --> 00:12:07,039
there is a very important message:

238
00:12:07,807 --> 00:12:08,575
that God would send a Savior.

239
00:12:10,623 --> 00:12:13,951
And this Savior would come to the earth twice.

240
00:12:13,951 --> 00:12:17,023
The Feasts of the LORD.

241
00:12:17,023 --> 00:12:22,655
It can also reveal God's own timetable, His calendar.

242
00:12:22,655 --> 00:12:30,079
It can reveal the two comings of the Savior whom God sends.

243
00:12:30,079 --> 00:12:33,151
We know that over two thousand years ago, the Lord Jesus came and became a man,

244
00:12:33,151 --> 00:12:35,740
and for our sake was hung upon the cross.

245
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:38,271
Then the Lord ascended into heaven,

246
00:12:38,271 --> 00:12:40,319
the Holy Spirit came down, and the church appeared.

247
00:12:41,599 --> 00:12:43,135
And so we come, right up

248
00:12:43,391 --> 00:12:44,159
to the present day,

249
00:12:44,671 --> 00:12:49,680
and what you see is that the Lord will keep His promise to come back and receive the church to Himself.

250
00:12:50,047 --> 00:12:51,583
In heaven there will be

251
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:54,000
the rewarding before the judgment seat of Christ, and the marriage feast of the Lamb,

252
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:56,640
while on the earth there will be seven years of great tribulation.

253
00:12:56,703 --> 00:13:01,567
And after those seven years, the Lord will descend together with us. You see,

254
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:04,383
this Savior comes to the earth two separate times.

255
00:13:04,639 --> 00:13:08,479
And this, in fact, is one of the very cores of biblical prophecy.

256
00:13:10,271 --> 00:13:11,295
As we were saying,

257
00:13:11,551 --> 00:13:12,831
these appointed feasts —

258
00:13:13,343 --> 00:13:18,463
these seven feasts — begin with the Passover, which falls in their first month,

259
00:13:18,975 --> 00:13:20,255
beginning on the fourteenth of that first month.

260
00:13:21,535 --> 00:13:27,679
And then, following right behind it, comes the Feast of Unleavened Bread. As we said, you'll notice it runs from the 15th to

261
00:13:27,935 --> 00:13:28,447
the 21st.

262
00:13:28,703 --> 00:13:31,519
The Feast of Unleavened Bread begins on the 14th,

263
00:13:32,031 --> 00:13:34,079
at sunset — that is, around six o'clock, it begins.

264
00:13:34,079 --> 00:13:37,745
The Passover is very special; in a little while, when we come to it, you'll understand it.

265
00:13:37,745 --> 00:13:40,719
After the Passover, following right behind it, comes the Feast of Unleavened Bread.

266
00:13:40,719 --> 00:13:43,600
But here's something fascinating — you'll notice that the Feast of Firstfruits has no fixed date,

267
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:46,623
and Pentecost has no fixed date either, because

268
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:48,159
each and every year it falls differently.

269
00:13:48,927 --> 00:13:52,255
So how is the Feast of Firstfruits reckoned? It is the day after

270
00:13:53,023 --> 00:13:55,583
the Sabbath that follows the Passover —

271
00:13:56,095 --> 00:13:57,119
that is the Feast of Firstfruits.

272
00:13:58,143 --> 00:14:00,959
And so you'll notice that between the Feast of Firstfruits and the Passover,

273
00:14:01,471 --> 00:14:04,031
there may be just one day, or there may be as many as seven days.

274
00:14:04,287 --> 00:14:08,383
It isn't fixed at all — it depends entirely on when the Passover itself happens to fall.

275
00:14:08,383 --> 00:14:11,440
So you'll find that the Feast of Firstfruits has no set date:

276
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,039
it is simply the day after the Sabbath that follows the Passover.

277
00:14:15,295 --> 00:14:17,087
And what, then, is Pentecost?

278
00:14:17,343 --> 00:14:19,135
It is, in fact, after the Feast of Firstfruits —

279
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:22,719
the day after seven Sabbaths,

280
00:14:22,719 --> 00:14:27,000
that is, seven sevens, which is forty-nine, plus one more day, making fifty.

281
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:32,160
So "Pentecost" means this — "pente" is fifty — fifty days later comes Pentecost.

282
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:37,880
From this you can see that the first four feasts are all connected together.

283
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:41,840
It all begins with the Passover.

284
00:14:41,919 --> 00:14:44,223
In English the Passover is called "Passover."

285
00:14:44,479 --> 00:14:45,503
You might find that rather curious —

286
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:50,367
what does "pass over" mean? It means to pass it by, to pass over it.

287
00:14:50,367 --> 00:14:52,772
So how was the Passover first instituted?

288
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:58,303
It was back in the day when the people of Israel were still slaves in Egypt. God called Moses

289
00:14:58,303 --> 00:15:01,880
to teach the people of Israel to keep the feast — let me read it to you.

290
00:15:02,143 --> 00:15:05,215
It says: The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt,

291
00:15:05,727 --> 00:15:06,751
telling them

292
00:15:07,007 --> 00:15:08,799
to set this month as their first month,

293
00:15:09,055 --> 00:15:10,079
the beginning of months, the first month of the year.

294
00:15:10,847 --> 00:15:16,991
It was the very day God would bring Israel out of Egypt, so God said to set this month

295
00:15:17,247 --> 00:15:17,759
as

296
00:15:18,015 --> 00:15:19,807
the beginning of the year.

297
00:15:21,087 --> 00:15:23,647
And on the tenth of that month, the first month,

298
00:15:23,903 --> 00:15:29,480
every household, every father's house, was to take a lamb,

299
00:15:29,535 --> 00:15:30,559
one lamb for each household.

300
00:15:30,559 --> 00:15:33,645
And this lamb had to meet certain requirements.

301
00:15:34,399 --> 00:15:35,679
It had to be without defect —

302
00:15:36,191 --> 00:15:40,799
not lame, not sick, a strong one-year-old

303
00:15:41,311 --> 00:15:42,335
male —

304
00:15:42,335 --> 00:15:46,640
a sheep would do, or a goat, but it had to be a male.

305
00:15:46,687 --> 00:15:48,991
After it was chosen on the tenth,

306
00:15:49,759 --> 00:15:51,039
right up until the fourteenth —

307
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:54,623
and why so strange? The 11th, the 12th, the 13th, the 14th —

308
00:15:54,879 --> 00:15:58,975
what were those days for? The household had a purpose: to watch whether this lamb

309
00:15:58,975 --> 00:16:03,560
met the requirements — would it walk with a limp,

310
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,561
or lie there all day long without moving?

311
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:09,727
They watched to see whether the lamb truly met the conditions just mentioned.

312
00:16:09,727 --> 00:16:12,287
And when everything was found to be in order,

313
00:16:12,287 --> 00:16:17,663
then at the twilight of the 14th of the first month — and when is twilight? It is from three o'clock to six —

314
00:16:17,663 --> 00:16:21,073
the people of Israel would kill this lamb.

315
00:16:21,073 --> 00:16:22,302
So the Passover is very special indeed.

316
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:29,183
You'd say the Passover is the 14th of the first month — yes, but in fact it is the twilight of the 14th, only a few hours.

317
00:16:30,975 --> 00:16:33,760
The Passover is the 14th of the first month, from three o'clock

318
00:16:34,047 --> 00:16:37,887
to six, the few hours of twilight — this was the appointed time.

319
00:16:38,143 --> 00:16:41,215
After the lamb was killed that day, what was done? Its blood

320
00:16:41,727 --> 00:16:44,799
was brushed onto the lintel of the house,

321
00:16:45,567 --> 00:16:47,359
and onto the two doorposts,

322
00:16:47,359 --> 00:16:52,886
and the whole lamb was roasted with fire.

323
00:16:53,503 --> 00:16:54,527
It could not be boiled.

324
00:16:54,783 --> 00:16:56,063
It could not be prepared any other way —

325
00:16:56,319 --> 00:16:58,367
however else you might cook it, no; the whole was roasted with fire.

326
00:16:58,623 --> 00:16:59,391
And then

327
00:16:59,647 --> 00:17:02,207
it was eaten together with unleavened bread and bitter herbs.

328
00:17:02,975 --> 00:17:04,767
But in fact, all of this is a foreshadowing.

329
00:17:04,767 --> 00:17:08,720
And what does it foreshadow? It foreshadows that God would send a Savior.

330
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,720
And this Savior would be just like this very lamb.

331
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:17,480
We know the Lord was crucified — was He not crowned with a crown of thorns,

332
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:21,480
shedding His blood, His two hands nailed fast to the cross?

333
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:24,480
So the blood was brushed on the lintel, and on the two doorposts.

334
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,247
You might ask,

335
00:17:25,247 --> 00:17:31,391
why was no blood put on the threshold below? This points to exactly this — that the Lord was lifted up,

336
00:17:31,903 --> 00:17:32,927
His feet lifted off the ground.

337
00:17:33,439 --> 00:17:37,535
And of course there is a meaning here too: the Lord's blood should never be trampled underfoot.

338
00:17:37,535 --> 00:17:42,019
The whole lamb was roasted with fire, enduring all of its agony.

339
00:17:42,399 --> 00:17:47,007
So you see what the focus of the Passover is: it is that lamb —

340
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:48,799
chosen from the tenth,

341
00:17:49,055 --> 00:17:49,823
set apart,

342
00:17:50,335 --> 00:17:51,359
and then, over those few days,

343
00:17:51,871 --> 00:17:53,663
verified and observed —

344
00:17:53,919 --> 00:17:54,687
was it without defect,

345
00:17:55,455 --> 00:17:56,479
was it strong and sound?

346
00:17:57,247 --> 00:18:00,319
And then, at the twilight of the 14th,

347
00:18:00,575 --> 00:18:01,599
it was killed,

348
00:18:01,599 --> 00:18:04,000
its blood brushed on the lintel and the doorposts,

349
00:18:04,159 --> 00:18:05,183
and then it was eaten.

350
00:18:05,439 --> 00:18:11,583
The lamb, the whole lamb, was roasted. To this very day the people of Israel still keep the Passover.

351
00:18:11,583 --> 00:18:16,800
So at the Passover meal there are bitter herbs, and unleavened bread,

352
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:22,800
and one special thing too: a shank bone of the lamb, the lamb's "arm."

353
00:18:22,847 --> 00:18:25,407
It has meaning too; in a little while, when we come to it, you'll understand.

354
00:18:27,455 --> 00:18:30,271
So for all of these many years they kept the Passover,

355
00:18:30,527 --> 00:18:31,295
always observing it in this very way,

356
00:18:31,295 --> 00:18:34,367
until one particular year —

357
00:18:34,367 --> 00:18:35,135
a very special year.

358
00:18:35,903 --> 00:18:38,975
For in the Bible there is the prophecy of the seventy sevens.

359
00:18:39,231 --> 00:18:45,375
It was the prophet Daniel, grieved to the heart that the people of Israel

360
00:18:45,631 --> 00:18:47,423
were constantly sinning and turning away from God,

361
00:18:47,679 --> 00:18:48,447
to the point of the nation's ruin.

362
00:18:48,703 --> 00:18:50,239
He made intercession on behalf of the people of Israel.

363
00:18:51,007 --> 00:18:54,079
And it turns out that when he prayed in this way, God responded.

364
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:55,871
I believe God's heart was deeply moved.

365
00:18:56,127 --> 00:18:58,175
And today, too, God is deeply responsive.

366
00:18:58,943 --> 00:19:04,575
Just as today, when you see so many people who are sick, or caught in the flames of war — God is in fact

367
00:19:04,831 --> 00:19:06,367
full of compassion, and He is deeply responsive.

368
00:19:06,367 --> 00:19:09,884
So God gave the prophecy of the seventy sevens,

369
00:19:10,207 --> 00:19:12,511
revealing it to this man Daniel.

370
00:19:13,279 --> 00:19:20,400
And how does it read? "Seventy weeks are determined for your people" — that is Israel — "and for your holy city" — that is Jerusalem.

371
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,727
It has a purpose:

372
00:19:21,727 --> 00:19:23,263
to finish the transgression,

373
00:19:23,775 --> 00:19:24,799
to make an end of sins,

374
00:19:25,311 --> 00:19:26,335
to make reconciliation for iniquity,

375
00:19:27,359 --> 00:19:31,199
to bring in everlasting righteousness, to seal up vision and prophecy, and to anoint the Most Holy.

376
00:19:31,711 --> 00:19:35,039
Now here there are, in fact, two sets of purposes.

377
00:19:35,551 --> 00:19:37,087
The first is to deal with sin —

378
00:19:37,087 --> 00:19:40,240
"to finish the transgression" is God's promise

379
00:19:40,671 --> 00:19:43,231
to give them power so that they would sin no more,

380
00:19:43,999 --> 00:19:47,071
and even "to make an end of sins" means that He would deal with all sin,

381
00:19:47,583 --> 00:19:48,863
every last trace of sin.

382
00:19:49,887 --> 00:19:50,911
He would do away with sin itself.

383
00:19:51,167 --> 00:19:55,519
"To make reconciliation for iniquity" means that all the consequences of sin,

384
00:19:56,287 --> 00:19:59,103
every price, He would repay, and clear it all away.

385
00:19:59,103 --> 00:20:02,555
Simply put: to deal with sin completely and utterly.

386
00:20:02,943 --> 00:20:06,015
"To bring in everlasting righteousness" — to bring in,

387
00:20:06,271 --> 00:20:08,063
or to manifest, everlasting righteousness.

388
00:20:08,575 --> 00:20:13,439
"To seal up vision and prophecy" — now in what situation do you seal something up? When it is finished.

389
00:20:13,695 --> 00:20:19,839
When a particular case is finished, when the file is complete, then you seal it. So in fact, "to seal up

390
00:20:20,095 --> 00:20:23,935
vision and prophecy" means, simply put, to fulfill the vision and the prophecy,

391
00:20:23,935 --> 00:20:25,988
"and to anoint the Most Holy."

392
00:20:26,495 --> 00:20:32,639
Now this prophecy of the seventy sevens — we mentioned it in one of our earlier special meetings, so I

393
00:20:32,895 --> 00:20:35,711
would encourage you, when you have the chance, to go back and watch it again, all right?

394
00:20:35,967 --> 00:20:42,111
It was the meeting of March 19th; you can find it on the church's YouTube channel.

395
00:20:42,111 --> 00:20:44,671
This prophecy of the seventy sevens —

396
00:20:44,671 --> 00:20:49,023
we'll present it here visually; the pictures you see show this same thing:

397
00:20:49,535 --> 00:20:51,583
that it emphasizes two times,

398
00:20:52,095 --> 00:20:53,887
namely the two comings

399
00:20:54,143 --> 00:20:58,495
of this Savior. At His first coming, He would

400
00:20:59,263 --> 00:21:00,031
finish the transgression,

401
00:21:01,311 --> 00:21:02,335
make an end of sins,

402
00:21:02,847 --> 00:21:04,127
and make reconciliation for iniquity —

403
00:21:04,383 --> 00:21:05,407
He would deal with sin.

404
00:21:05,407 --> 00:21:09,344
At His second coming, He would bring in everlasting righteousness,

405
00:21:10,271 --> 00:21:12,063
fulfill every vision and prophecy,

406
00:21:12,575 --> 00:21:13,855
and anoint the Most Holy.

407
00:21:14,367 --> 00:21:15,647
So do you see it now?

408
00:21:16,672 --> 00:21:21,792
Because the Savior comes two times, this is a central focus of biblical prophecy.

409
00:21:23,584 --> 00:21:24,352
And so this time,

410
00:21:24,608 --> 00:21:30,752
we won't go into the whole of the seventy sevens in detail, as I said at the start; you can listen back to the earlier

411
00:21:30,752 --> 00:21:33,708
special meeting. But I want you to notice a few things. What does it say?

412
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:37,664
"Seventy weeks are determined — so know this, and understand it —

413
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:44,064
from the going forth of the command to restore and build Jerusalem, until Messiah the Prince,

414
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:46,624
there shall be seven sevens and sixty-two sevens."

415
00:21:46,624 --> 00:21:51,209
It says that even in troublesome times, Jerusalem, both street and wall, shall be rebuilt.

416
00:21:51,488 --> 00:21:53,024
"And after the sixty-two sevens,

417
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:56,096
Messiah shall be cut off, and shall have nothing" —

418
00:21:56,096 --> 00:21:58,677
"and shall have nothing" — beyond the plain sense of having nothing left,

419
00:21:58,677 --> 00:22:00,319
it in fact also carries this meaning:

420
00:22:01,472 --> 00:22:02,752
"not for Himself."

421
00:22:03,264 --> 00:22:04,800
That is, He would be cut off

422
00:22:05,056 --> 00:22:07,360
not for any cause of His own.

423
00:22:10,432 --> 00:22:12,480
All right, so it speaks of Messiah the Prince.

424
00:22:12,992 --> 00:22:14,016
Now it turns out

425
00:22:14,528 --> 00:22:20,672
that among the people of Israel, there were three kinds of people who were anointed — meaning that at their inauguration,

426
00:22:20,928 --> 00:22:22,976
anointing oil would be poured upon their head.

427
00:22:22,976 --> 00:22:25,259
And which three kinds of people? They are

428
00:22:25,259 --> 00:22:30,240
the king, the priest, and the prophet.

429
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:33,752
Upon them the anointing oil would be poured.

430
00:22:33,752 --> 00:22:35,776
And what else does this say?

431
00:22:35,776 --> 00:22:41,920
It says: from the going forth of the command to restore and build Jerusalem, until Messiah the Prince appears, there shall be seven sevens and

432
00:22:42,176 --> 00:22:42,688
sixty-two sevens.

433
00:22:42,688 --> 00:22:44,992
This picture shows it to you.

434
00:22:44,992 --> 00:22:45,760
Seven weeks —

435
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:51,392
after these forty-nine years, Jerusalem, both street and wall, was rebuilt.

436
00:22:51,648 --> 00:22:55,744
And after a further sixty-two sevens, making sixty-nine sevens in all — and this comes to four hundred

437
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:56,768
and eighty-three years.

438
00:22:57,024 --> 00:23:01,888
After these 483 years had passed, that Anointed One would appear.

439
00:23:04,192 --> 00:23:05,216
The Jewish

440
00:23:05,728 --> 00:23:11,872
calendar works like this: their year is 360 days, and so 483 years, in fact,

441
00:23:12,128 --> 00:23:14,688
amounts to 173,880 days.

442
00:23:15,712 --> 00:23:18,528
Now the solar year that we speak of today,

443
00:23:18,784 --> 00:23:19,552
the solar calendar,

444
00:23:19,808 --> 00:23:22,368
is in fact 365 days,

445
00:23:23,136 --> 00:23:25,184
and about a quarter more.

446
00:23:27,232 --> 00:23:32,608
After careful study, when was this command to restore and build Jerusalem issued?

447
00:23:32,864 --> 00:23:33,888
At that time,

448
00:23:34,144 --> 00:23:40,288
Persia had an emperor who issued the command to build Jerusalem, and it was in

449
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:41,824
444 BC, on the 5th of March.

450
00:23:41,824 --> 00:23:43,824
Starting from that very day,

451
00:23:44,128 --> 00:23:45,408
if you add on

452
00:23:45,664 --> 00:23:47,712
173,880 days,

453
00:23:48,224 --> 00:23:48,736
you arrive

454
00:23:48,992 --> 00:23:51,552
at AD 33,

455
00:23:51,808 --> 00:23:53,088
on the 30th of March.

456
00:23:53,344 --> 00:23:55,136
And what was happening on that very day?

457
00:23:56,672 --> 00:23:58,720
On that day, it turns out, the Lord Jesus,

458
00:24:00,512 --> 00:24:01,792
in the identity of a King,

459
00:24:02,304 --> 00:24:03,584
entered into Jerusalem,

460
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:05,632
on the last leg of His journey.

461
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:09,216
At that time He told His disciples

462
00:24:09,472 --> 00:24:10,752
to untie a donkey,

463
00:24:11,776 --> 00:24:12,800
and He rode up upon it —

464
00:24:13,056 --> 00:24:19,200
the colt of a donkey, a little donkey.

465
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:21,000
And the crowds lining the road cheered,

466
00:24:21,248 --> 00:24:22,016
welcoming Him, treating Him as their King.

467
00:24:22,016 --> 00:24:26,368
And this, it turns out, bore witness to,

468
00:24:26,368 --> 00:24:28,672
and fulfilled, this very saying of the Bible,

469
00:24:29,184 --> 00:24:32,000
in the book of Zechariah, 500 BC —

470
00:24:32,256 --> 00:24:34,304
500 years before the Lord Jesus came,

471
00:24:34,304 --> 00:24:36,227
there was this saying:

472
00:24:36,227 --> 00:24:38,394
"Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion!

473
00:24:39,424 --> 00:24:41,728
Shout, O daughter of Jerusalem!

474
00:24:41,984 --> 00:24:44,032
Behold, your King is coming to you;

475
00:24:44,288 --> 00:24:46,592
He is just and endowed with salvation,

476
00:24:46,592 --> 00:24:50,432
lowly, and riding on a donkey,

477
00:24:50,432 --> 00:24:52,224
a colt, the foal of a donkey."

478
00:24:53,504 --> 00:24:59,648
And indeed the Lord Jesus, riding on a donkey's colt, entered Jerusalem, fulfilling this very saying,

479
00:24:59,904 --> 00:25:00,672
and showing what?

480
00:25:00,928 --> 00:25:04,256
That He is the King who was to come — He is that very King.

481
00:25:06,304 --> 00:25:07,584
People have carefully researched it,

482
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:09,888
and as I said a moment ago, that very day

483
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:11,680
was precisely

484
00:25:12,192 --> 00:25:13,216
the 30th of March,

485
00:25:13,472 --> 00:25:15,008
AD 33.

486
00:25:16,544 --> 00:25:18,336
So you find that from the command to

487
00:25:18,592 --> 00:25:21,920
rebuild Jerusalem until the appearing of the Anointed One,

488
00:25:22,688 --> 00:25:26,784
the Lord's riding into Jerusalem on a donkey, it was precisely sixty-nine sevens of years.

489
00:25:26,784 --> 00:25:30,574
But that day was very special.

490
00:25:30,624 --> 00:25:32,672
That day was also, in that year,

491
00:25:32,928 --> 00:25:34,976
the tenth of the first month on the Jewish calendar.

492
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:37,536
And what does that mean?

493
00:25:37,792 --> 00:25:41,800
It was the very day the Passover lamb was to be selected.

494
00:25:42,144 --> 00:25:48,032
So the Lord Jesus riding into Jerusalem on a donkey also showed what He is: He is the Lamb of God.

495
00:25:48,032 --> 00:25:52,514
So you find that after He entered Jerusalem,

496
00:25:52,514 --> 00:25:54,674
He did not die at once.

497
00:25:54,674 --> 00:25:58,016
There were several days, and in those days

498
00:25:58,016 --> 00:26:03,136
He was verified to be that perfect Son of Man, the spotless Lamb of God.

499
00:26:03,648 --> 00:26:07,232
And when it came to the twilight of the 14th of the first month,

500
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,024
the Lord died.

501
00:26:11,072 --> 00:26:14,400
Upon the cross, He committed His spirit into His Father's hands.

502
00:26:16,192 --> 00:26:16,960
And this also

503
00:26:17,472 --> 00:26:21,824
fulfilled the latter part of the seventy sevens: "and after the sixty-two sevens" —

504
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,384
after the 30th of March,

505
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:25,152
afterward,

506
00:26:25,408 --> 00:26:28,224
a few days later, the Anointed One was cut off.

507
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,016
The Lord Jesus was hung upon the tree,

508
00:26:30,528 --> 00:26:33,600
having nothing. And it turns out that the Lord, in His dying,

509
00:26:33,856 --> 00:26:36,416
did not die for Himself, not for any cause of His own.

510
00:26:39,488 --> 00:26:45,632
So you'll find that the Bible gives no small space to recording what happened in those few days after the Lord Jesus rode into Jerusalem.

511
00:26:46,656 --> 00:26:48,192
And what happened in those few days

512
00:26:48,448 --> 00:26:53,056
was, in fact, to let us know that He is the Lamb of God, that He is the One without blemish.

513
00:26:53,824 --> 00:26:54,848
Let me give you an example.

514
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:56,640
There was an occasion —

515
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,200
that day was, I believe,

516
00:26:59,712 --> 00:27:01,504
a Wednesday —

517
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,296
when some people came and questioned the Lord.

518
00:27:03,552 --> 00:27:09,696
Here it tells of a spy; as it says just before, they wanted to get

519
00:27:09,952 --> 00:27:15,840
some handle against Him by testing Him, to catch something in the Lord's words with which to attack Him.

520
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:18,346
So some spies questioned the Lord, saying, "Teacher,

521
00:27:19,936 --> 00:27:23,008
we know that what You say and teach is right,

522
00:27:23,264 --> 00:27:24,288
and that You do not

523
00:27:24,544 --> 00:27:25,824
show personal favoritism,

524
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:27,872
but teach the way of God in truth.

525
00:27:28,384 --> 00:27:31,968
Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?"

526
00:27:32,736 --> 00:27:33,504
You'd think, well,

527
00:27:34,272 --> 00:27:36,320
that sounds rather sincere.

528
00:27:36,832 --> 00:27:40,160
But let me tell you — that opening was not praise of the Lord at all.

529
00:27:40,928 --> 00:27:43,232
In fact, they were cutting off the Lord's every way of escape.

530
00:27:44,256 --> 00:27:46,560
Because, you see, before this incident,

531
00:27:46,816 --> 00:27:48,608
some people had already

532
00:27:48,864 --> 00:27:49,632
challenged the Lord, questioning Him.

533
00:27:51,168 --> 00:27:53,216
They said, when You entered Jerusalem

534
00:27:53,472 --> 00:27:54,240
and went to the temple,

535
00:27:54,496 --> 00:27:59,104
and cleansed the temple, overturning those who sold cattle and sheep — they asked Him,

536
00:27:59,360 --> 00:28:01,920
"By what authority do You do these things?" And the Lord asked them in return,

537
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:09,040
"The baptism of John — by what authority was it; from where did it come?"

538
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:10,880
And those people reasoned among themselves.

539
00:28:11,136 --> 00:28:17,280
They thought, if we say John's baptism was from heaven, the Lord will say,

540
00:28:17,536 --> 00:28:18,304
"Why then did you not believe him?"

541
00:28:19,328 --> 00:28:20,608
"Why did you not believe him?

542
00:28:20,608 --> 00:28:23,277
You believe John was from God — why then do you not believe that I am from God?"

543
00:28:23,277 --> 00:28:30,336
But if they said John's baptism was of men, not from God, they feared the people,

544
00:28:30,336 --> 00:28:32,640
for the people held John to be a prophet.

545
00:28:34,688 --> 00:28:35,712
So they said to the Lord, "We do not know," and would not answer.

546
00:28:37,248 --> 00:28:43,392
So you see that these spies were not praising the Lord at all; they were cutting off His escape.

547
00:28:43,648 --> 00:28:49,024
They said, "We know that You are true, that what You teach is right, that You show no partiality and do not regard the appearance of men."

548
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:52,864
And then they asked their question — it was just one question, very simple:

549
00:28:53,120 --> 00:28:53,888
they asked,

550
00:28:54,144 --> 00:28:55,936
"Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?"

551
00:28:56,448 --> 00:28:58,240
It really is that simple a question.

552
00:28:59,264 --> 00:29:02,336
But do not underestimate it — this question is not at all easy to answer,

553
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:06,688
because whichever way you answer, you run into trouble; you are finished.

554
00:29:06,944 --> 00:29:07,712
And why is that?

555
00:29:07,968 --> 00:29:08,992
Because if you say

556
00:29:09,504 --> 00:29:11,552
one ought to pay taxes to Caesar,

557
00:29:11,808 --> 00:29:13,088
then those Jews would say,

558
00:29:14,368 --> 00:29:17,696
"You are surely a traitor" — that is, you're encouraging

559
00:29:17,952 --> 00:29:23,584
the Romans to rule over the Jews, since you would have the Jews pay their taxes to Caesar.

560
00:29:24,608 --> 00:29:25,632
Wouldn't that then make you

561
00:29:25,888 --> 00:29:30,752
a Jewish traitor, a collaborator?

562
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:37,152
But if the Lord said not to pay taxes to Caesar, those others would say He was inciting rebellion, stirring up the Jews

563
00:29:37,408 --> 00:29:40,680
to resist the Romans.

564
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:42,272
So do you see how hard this question is?

565
00:29:42,272 --> 00:29:45,629
But how did the Lord answer it? He said —

566
00:29:45,629 --> 00:29:49,628
the Lord saw through their trickery, and said, "Bring Me a coin.

567
00:29:49,628 --> 00:29:54,214
Whose image and inscription is this?"

568
00:29:54,214 --> 00:29:57,130
Those people said, "Caesar's."

569
00:29:57,130 --> 00:30:01,204
On the coin was Caesar's image.

570
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:04,032
Then the Lord said, "The things that are Caesar's, render to Caesar;

571
00:30:05,056 --> 00:30:05,824
and likewise,

572
00:30:06,336 --> 00:30:07,872
the things that are God's, render to God."

573
00:30:09,664 --> 00:30:10,944
What a fine answer that was.

574
00:30:12,736 --> 00:30:16,832
And what was the reaction of the people there? They marveled.

575
00:30:17,088 --> 00:30:17,856
That is,

576
00:30:18,112 --> 00:30:19,648
His answer, His response —

577
00:30:19,648 --> 00:30:24,800
true to form, His answer gave them no handle with which to accuse the Lord.

578
00:30:26,304 --> 00:30:30,400
They fell silent, unable to speak. And so, from this, you can see that what happened in those few days

579
00:30:30,656 --> 00:30:33,216
proved the Lord's wisdom,

580
00:30:33,472 --> 00:30:34,240
His perfection —

581
00:30:34,496 --> 00:30:36,288
that He is indeed the spotless Lamb of God.

582
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:42,944
So a few days later, when the Lord was nailed to the cross, He did not die in some muddled, senseless way.

583
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:47,552
Looking at this matter of the cross, you come to know that the Lord is truly full of wisdom.

584
00:30:50,368 --> 00:30:51,648
Our topic today,

585
00:30:52,672 --> 00:30:53,952
"At the Appointed Time,"

586
00:30:55,232 --> 00:30:56,512
is in fact a verse of Scripture.

587
00:30:57,024 --> 00:30:58,304
In the book of Romans it says this.

588
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,864
It says: for when we were still without strength,

589
00:31:01,376 --> 00:31:01,888
Christ,

590
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,936
at the appointed time,

591
00:31:04,192 --> 00:31:05,472
died for sinners.

592
00:31:08,544 --> 00:31:10,080
It turns out that this appointed time

593
00:31:10,848 --> 00:31:11,872
was set by God.

594
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:15,968
It was set for His Son, for the Lord Jesus Christ.

595
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:18,784
It was the Lord Jesus who, at the appointed time,

596
00:31:19,552 --> 00:31:20,832
died for sinners.

597
00:31:21,344 --> 00:31:23,136
It says: scarcely for a righteous man will one die;

598
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:25,440
yet for a good man, perhaps one would even dare to die.

599
00:31:26,464 --> 00:31:27,488
But Christ —

600
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:30,560
while we were still sinners,

601
00:31:31,328 --> 00:31:32,352
died for us.

602
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:33,888
The love of God

603
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,424
is, right here,

604
00:31:35,936 --> 00:31:36,960
shown toward us.

605
00:31:39,264 --> 00:31:40,544
Sin is committed by people —

606
00:31:41,824 --> 00:31:43,872
each who sins bears his own guilt, doesn't he?

607
00:31:44,384 --> 00:31:50,016
But while we were still sinners, still sinning and offending God, God actually

608
00:31:50,528 --> 00:31:53,600
prepared His Son for us, prepared this Savior for us,

609
00:31:54,880 --> 00:32:01,024
and when the Lord died for us in this way, while we were still sinners — you see,

610
00:32:01,280 --> 00:32:02,304
this is the very love of God.

611
00:32:05,376 --> 00:32:06,656
This picture tells

612
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:08,704
a truth,

613
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:11,264
the very situation that so many people face today.

614
00:32:12,032 --> 00:32:13,568
A moment ago you said God is so real,

615
00:32:13,824 --> 00:32:14,592
and so good —

616
00:32:14,848 --> 00:32:16,384
so why can't I feel Him?

617
00:32:16,384 --> 00:32:20,035
Why can't I experience Him?

618
00:32:20,035 --> 00:32:21,843
It turns out there is a wall between God and man,

619
00:32:21,843 --> 00:32:24,271
a very thick wall. And what does the Bible say?

620
00:32:25,856 --> 00:32:26,368
Our sins

621
00:32:26,624 --> 00:32:28,160
have separated us from God.

622
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:30,878
Not merely separated us — but cut us off completely.

623
00:32:33,024 --> 00:32:34,560
And this wall is the wall of sin.

624
00:32:35,584 --> 00:32:36,608
You might say,

625
00:32:37,120 --> 00:32:38,656
but I've never murdered or set fires,

626
00:32:39,680 --> 00:32:40,704
I've never robbed or plundered.

627
00:32:41,472 --> 00:32:44,800
Murder, arson, robbery, and plunder are the worst of all —

628
00:32:46,080 --> 00:32:47,616
but what does the Bible say sin is?

629
00:32:48,128 --> 00:32:50,432
It is anything at all that goes against the conscience.

630
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:52,224
You clearly know what is right,

631
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,504
and yet you don't do it;

632
00:32:54,016 --> 00:32:55,296
you clearly know what is wrong,

633
00:32:55,552 --> 00:32:56,576
and yet you go ahead and do it anyway.

634
00:32:56,832 --> 00:32:57,856
These are your sins.

635
00:32:58,624 --> 00:33:00,928
So it's a fascinating thing — people have a conscience.

636
00:33:01,184 --> 00:33:03,232
You don't need to raise your hand

637
00:33:03,488 --> 00:33:06,816
during an exam and ask the teacher, "Is it wrong for me to cheat?" You don't need to ask.

638
00:33:08,096 --> 00:33:09,376
It isn't something you ever learned out of a book.

639
00:33:10,656 --> 00:33:12,960
At home you don't need to raise your hand and ask your mother,

640
00:33:13,216 --> 00:33:15,520
"Mom, is it wrong for me to steal your money?" You don't need to ask — you already know.

641
00:33:17,056 --> 00:33:20,128
Anything that goes against the conscience is sin.

642
00:33:21,408 --> 00:33:24,992
And the most terrible thing about sin is this: you cannot take it back again.

643
00:33:26,016 --> 00:33:28,064
You tell a lie to deceive someone — fine;

644
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:31,392
but when you find out that someone has lied to deceive you, oh, your temper flares right up.

645
00:33:34,976 --> 00:33:36,256
Some people say,

646
00:33:36,512 --> 00:33:39,328
a man who isn't a bit of a rogue wastes his youth;

647
00:33:40,352 --> 00:33:42,912
having a mistress is quite an ordinary thing, they say.

648
00:33:42,912 --> 00:33:45,984
But if his wife were to tell him

649
00:33:45,984 --> 00:33:50,080
that she too had a lover on the side — oh, it might really be that,

650
00:33:50,848 --> 00:33:51,360
it might really be that,

651
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:53,920
there's no telling what would happen.

652
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:56,992
So you find that the terror of sin

653
00:33:56,992 --> 00:33:58,528
is that it goes against the conscience.

654
00:33:59,552 --> 00:34:03,136
The terror of sin is its self-centeredness, and that you cannot take it back.

655
00:34:03,136 --> 00:34:10,191
Sin is like a heavy burden pressing down upon a person; and that chain below — do you see it?

656
00:34:10,191 --> 00:34:12,903
I believe everyone wants to be good.

657
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:16,704
I once met a man who cursed terribly.

658
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:19,008
He resolved to change,

659
00:34:19,264 --> 00:34:21,056
and for a day, then two days, he managed it;

660
00:34:21,312 --> 00:34:22,336
but when the third day came,

661
00:34:22,336 --> 00:34:27,320
he cursed again, and even worse than he had before.

662
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:31,000
I believe everyone wants to be good, but to sin is to become a slave to sin,

663
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:32,320
unable ever to be free.

664
00:34:33,344 --> 00:34:34,880
And to sin brings death as well.

665
00:34:36,416 --> 00:34:40,000
Some illnesses today are brought on by sin,

666
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:43,328
and some deaths are brought on by sin.

667
00:34:43,584 --> 00:34:47,168
And death is not the end of it; after death, one must face the judgment of God.

668
00:34:47,680 --> 00:34:50,752
All who sin, God will cast into hell.

669
00:34:51,264 --> 00:34:53,824
If God could make a sun that burns for so many years,

670
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:55,616
then of course He is also able to make

671
00:34:55,872 --> 00:35:00,480
a hell, a lake of fire that is never quenched, into which all who sin

672
00:35:00,992 --> 00:35:02,016
will be cast.

673
00:35:04,576 --> 00:35:07,136
When the Lord Jesus came, at His first coming,

674
00:35:07,392 --> 00:35:09,440
it was to deal with our sin.

675
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:11,744
And so, in

676
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,792
the seventh century BC,

677
00:35:13,792 --> 00:35:15,948
seven hundred years before the Lord Jesus was born,

678
00:35:15,948 --> 00:35:19,193
in the book of Isaiah there are these words.

679
00:35:19,424 --> 00:35:20,448
It says: just as many

680
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:21,728
were astonished at Him —

681
00:35:21,984 --> 00:35:22,496
astonished —

682
00:35:24,032 --> 00:35:26,080
His visage was marred more than any other man,

683
00:35:26,592 --> 00:35:27,360
and His form

684
00:35:27,616 --> 00:35:28,896
more than the sons of men;

685
00:35:29,664 --> 00:35:30,176
so,

686
00:35:30,432 --> 00:35:32,480
He shall sprinkle many nations;

687
00:35:32,992 --> 00:35:34,528
kings shall shut their mouths at Him.

688
00:35:34,528 --> 00:35:37,600
This speaks of one who suffers.

689
00:35:37,600 --> 00:35:38,880
And who exactly is this?

690
00:35:39,392 --> 00:35:45,536
When people saw Him they were astonished — "astonishing," truly alarmed. And why? Because His

691
00:35:45,792 --> 00:35:47,072
face was so terribly marred.

692
00:35:47,072 --> 00:35:51,039
In fact, this is speaking of the Lord Jesus' final days.

693
00:35:52,448 --> 00:35:53,472
After the Lord was seized,

694
00:35:53,984 --> 00:35:55,008
He was dragged away all through the night,

695
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:56,800
tried in five different places,

696
00:35:56,800 --> 00:36:00,801
because they were set on condemning the Lord to death before daybreak,

697
00:36:00,801 --> 00:36:02,855
to do away with Him.

698
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:04,992
So all night long He had no sleep,

699
00:36:05,248 --> 00:36:08,832
passing through trial after trial, torment after torment.

700
00:36:09,088 --> 00:36:11,904
And then, "His form more marred than the sons of men" —

701
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:17,024
what this means is His body, His form, His very "form,"

702
00:36:18,048 --> 00:36:19,328
was abused

703
00:36:19,584 --> 00:36:25,728
and beaten until it was not like a man's — more than a man — meaning His appearance, at a single glance,

704
00:36:25,984 --> 00:36:26,752
no longer looked like a man at all.

705
00:36:26,752 --> 00:36:29,189
And what exactly happened?

706
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:31,872
That day was, in fact, the Passover.

707
00:36:32,896 --> 00:36:39,040
The governor at the time was Pilate; the Jews dragged the Lord before Pilate,

708
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:42,040
and Pilate interrogated the Lord, but could find no fault in Him at all.

709
00:36:42,368 --> 00:36:46,976
So once, twice, three times he said, I can find no fault in Him.

710
00:36:47,488 --> 00:36:49,024
What do you want me to do with Him?

711
00:36:49,024 --> 00:36:52,608
Then Pilate thought of a method.

712
00:36:52,608 --> 00:36:54,912
At the Passover there was a custom

713
00:36:55,168 --> 00:36:57,472
that he could release one prisoner.

714
00:36:58,496 --> 00:37:04,128
And he knew the Jews had seized Jesus out of envy,

715
00:37:05,152 --> 00:37:07,968
not because Jesus had done anything worthy of death.

716
00:37:08,992 --> 00:37:15,136
So he thought of a method: he had Jesus scourged by the soldiers.

717
00:37:15,904 --> 00:37:17,920
Those whips were called the cat-o'-nine-tails —

718
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:21,920
a single whip splitting into nine, with metal on the tips.

719
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,640
When it struck, it would sink deep into the flesh.

720
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:29,120
There were records of some who, after such a beating, didn't even need to be crucified. And why?

721
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:31,264
you could even see the intestines, because the back

722
00:37:31,520 --> 00:37:32,288
has so little flesh on it.

723
00:37:32,288 --> 00:37:35,565
And what was the purpose of beating Him?

724
00:37:35,565 --> 00:37:38,405
It was to win the people's sympathy.

725
00:37:38,405 --> 00:37:42,272
So the Bible mentions again and again that the Lord Jesus was scourged,

726
00:37:42,272 --> 00:37:44,320
and all the more severely.

727
00:37:45,856 --> 00:37:47,648
He had committed no sin,

728
00:37:48,672 --> 00:37:50,208
yet people treated Him as a criminal —

729
00:37:50,976 --> 00:37:54,560
and even so, He did not receive even the treatment a criminal ought to have,

730
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:57,347
for He had to be beaten all the more severely.

731
00:37:57,376 --> 00:38:01,472
After the beating, Pilate brought the Lord Jesus out and said, "Behold the man!"

732
00:38:02,752 --> 00:38:04,288
And at that time,

733
00:38:04,544 --> 00:38:07,616
the Lord's form was marred more than the sons of men — that is what it means.

734
00:38:08,128 --> 00:38:09,920
Do you still remember that lamb?

735
00:38:10,432 --> 00:38:11,712
It could not be boiled in water;

736
00:38:11,968 --> 00:38:13,760
the whole of it had to be roasted with fire.

737
00:38:14,784 --> 00:38:19,392
This shows all the pain, all the torment, that the Lord passed through for us.

738
00:38:20,416 --> 00:38:21,440
And in the Bible,

739
00:38:21,696 --> 00:38:23,232
in the Psalms there is a saying like this.

740
00:38:23,488 --> 00:38:24,512
What does it say? It says —

741
00:38:25,024 --> 00:38:25,536
it says,

742
00:38:25,792 --> 00:38:26,560
my back —

743
00:38:26,816 --> 00:38:28,608
as if it were a plow,

744
00:38:28,864 --> 00:38:33,472
plowing upon my back, just like a man plowing a field, plowing upon the back,

745
00:38:33,728 --> 00:38:36,032
and the furrows they plowed were very long.

746
00:38:37,824 --> 00:38:39,616
I believe this is speaking of this very thing.

747
00:38:42,176 --> 00:38:45,504
So after Isaiah chapter 52,

748
00:38:45,504 --> 00:38:47,552
there is a saying like this.

749
00:38:47,552 --> 00:38:48,064
What does it say?

750
00:38:48,576 --> 00:38:49,856
It says: who has believed

751
00:38:50,112 --> 00:38:51,136
our report?

752
00:38:51,136 --> 00:38:53,440
And the arm of the LORD,

753
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,720
to whom has it been revealed?

754
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:58,933
The Lord Jesus, in the identity of a King, entered Jerusalem;

755
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:02,144
who could ever have imagined that a few days later He would come to such a state?

756
00:39:02,912 --> 00:39:07,008
So there is a saying below — earlier it said that kings

757
00:39:07,520 --> 00:39:08,800
would shut their mouths at Him,

758
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:11,872
because never before had a king, for his

759
00:39:11,872 --> 00:39:12,896
people,

760
00:39:13,408 --> 00:39:14,432
come to such a state.

761
00:39:15,200 --> 00:39:15,968
But He,

762
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:19,040
His form marred, His face so haggard,

763
00:39:19,296 --> 00:39:21,344
He washed many nations clean.

764
00:39:21,344 --> 00:39:25,906
And this, too, is the arm of the LORD.

765
00:39:26,720 --> 00:39:30,560
It turns out that God stretched out His arm to save us from sin,

766
00:39:32,096 --> 00:39:33,632
to lift us up out of the miry pit.

767
00:39:33,632 --> 00:39:41,568
And it turns out the word "arm" is the very same word as the shank bone of the Passover lamb —

768
00:39:41,568 --> 00:39:42,848
that is, His own arm.

769
00:39:45,152 --> 00:39:45,920
After the beating,

770
00:39:46,944 --> 00:39:53,088
Pilate thought those people would stop there — I can find no fault in Him, yet I've had Him beaten like this.

771
00:39:53,344 --> 00:39:54,112
"Behold the man!"

772
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,928
But what did the Jews do?

773
00:39:57,184 --> 00:39:57,696
They said,

774
00:39:58,208 --> 00:39:58,976
"Crucify Him!

775
00:39:59,744 --> 00:40:00,768
Crucify Him!"

776
00:40:02,560 --> 00:40:04,864
They would rather have a robber

777
00:40:04,864 --> 00:40:05,888
than have Jesus.

778
00:40:07,936 --> 00:40:09,984
And the more they cried out, the louder it grew.

779
00:40:10,496 --> 00:40:12,544
Pilate, seeing there was nothing to be done,

780
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:14,848
handed Jesus over

781
00:40:15,104 --> 00:40:16,640
to the soldiers to be crucified.

782
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:20,992
And what is crucifixion?

783
00:40:20,992 --> 00:40:23,040
A nail as thick as a silver coin,

784
00:40:23,552 --> 00:40:24,576
some nine inches long —

785
00:40:25,088 --> 00:40:27,392
three nails driven through the two hands

786
00:40:27,648 --> 00:40:28,160
and the two feet,

787
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:30,720
hanging a man of over a hundred pounds

788
00:40:30,720 --> 00:40:31,488
upon the wood.

789
00:40:34,048 --> 00:40:36,608
It is, in fact, a most cruel punishment. And why?

790
00:40:36,608 --> 00:40:38,608
Because crucifixion does not kill at once.

791
00:40:38,608 --> 00:40:41,560
The blood keeps flowing,

792
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:44,764
and as He is nailed there, His weight pulls Him forward.

793
00:40:45,056 --> 00:40:47,616
And you know, when your weight pulls you forward,

794
00:40:47,872 --> 00:40:48,896
you cannot draw breath.

795
00:40:49,152 --> 00:40:51,968
So in order to breathe, you have to push yourself up with all your strength;

796
00:40:51,968 --> 00:40:55,552
and when you push yourself up,

797
00:40:55,552 --> 00:40:57,344
your back, already beaten to shreds,

798
00:40:59,136 --> 00:41:03,488
that raw, shredded back is dragged up against the wood full of splinters,

799
00:41:03,744 --> 00:41:09,888
and with every movement, the wounds, the wounds from the nails, are pulled wider and longer, wider and longer.

800
00:41:11,168 --> 00:41:14,240
In fact, on the cross, you could say that every breath,

801
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:16,288
every gasp for air,

802
00:41:16,544 --> 00:41:17,568
is agony.

803
00:41:21,408 --> 00:41:22,432
And in this very way,

804
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:24,480
the Lord Jesus, from nine o'clock in the morning,

805
00:41:26,016 --> 00:41:28,064
hung there all the way until three in the afternoon.

806
00:41:29,088 --> 00:41:30,624
Now by rights

807
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,416
it should have been daytime, bright with sun;

808
00:41:32,416 --> 00:41:35,462
but at twelve noon, the whole land turned dark.

809
00:41:35,744 --> 00:41:36,768
It was as if God

810
00:41:37,024 --> 00:41:38,560
wanted people to take notice of this thing —

811
00:41:39,072 --> 00:41:42,400
to look upon this Savior crucified upon the cross.

812
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:47,193
The whole land turning dark is, of course, deeply meaningful too.

813
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:50,080
For the sun represents righteousness;

814
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:54,431
yet at that very moment, when there was no righteousness at all, the One least deserving to die

815
00:41:54,687 --> 00:41:55,455
was the very One who died.

816
00:41:59,295 --> 00:42:02,111
And when He had hung there until three in the afternoon,

817
00:42:02,111 --> 00:42:03,135
the Lord cried out with a loud voice:

818
00:42:03,135 --> 00:42:07,231
"My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?"

819
00:42:07,743 --> 00:42:10,303
It turns out that in that moment, it was not only the agony of the cross;

820
00:42:10,559 --> 00:42:13,119
the Father too stretched out His hand

821
00:42:13,631 --> 00:42:14,399
to strike Him,

822
00:42:14,655 --> 00:42:15,679
to punish His own Son.

823
00:42:18,239 --> 00:42:19,263
And then

824
00:42:19,775 --> 00:42:21,055
the Lord cried out with a loud voice,

825
00:42:21,567 --> 00:42:22,847
and He said, "It is finished."

826
00:42:23,103 --> 00:42:24,383
Then He bowed His head

827
00:42:24,639 --> 00:42:26,175
and committed His spirit to God.

828
00:42:27,711 --> 00:42:28,735
And at that time it was just past three o'clock —

829
00:42:28,991 --> 00:42:31,295
the very time for the slaughtering of the lamb,

830
00:42:32,063 --> 00:42:33,343
the very time of the Passover —

831
00:42:35,903 --> 00:42:37,439
representing the Lord,

832
00:42:37,695 --> 00:42:39,487
for us upon the cross,

833
00:42:40,255 --> 00:42:41,023
at the very moment of His death.

834
00:42:43,071 --> 00:42:45,800
The Chinese character 來, "to come," is deeply meaningful.

835
00:42:45,887 --> 00:42:48,447
The character 來 has a cross right in the middle of it.

836
00:42:48,959 --> 00:42:51,007
And then all people

837
00:42:51,263 --> 00:42:52,799
ought to come to the foot of the cross.

838
00:42:58,175 --> 00:43:01,247
And so, going on from here, I would like to share a hymn with you all.

839
00:43:01,503 --> 00:43:02,783
The name of this hymn

840
00:43:03,295 --> 00:43:06,040
is "Come, Please Feel."

841
00:43:06,623 --> 00:43:08,927
Let us go together to the foot of the cross,

842
00:43:09,183 --> 00:43:11,487
and see this Jesus, and all that He passed through for us.

843
00:43:11,487 --> 00:43:14,047
All that He passed through for us

844
00:43:14,047 --> 00:43:14,815
was not for Himself,

845
00:43:14,815 --> 00:43:17,200
but was for us.

846
00:48:06,911 --> 00:48:09,215
At the very end of the hymn there is a line —

847
00:48:09,727 --> 00:48:10,239
from the Bible.

848
00:48:10,751 --> 00:48:12,287
It says: He loved me

849
00:48:13,055 --> 00:48:14,079
and gave Himself for me.

850
00:48:15,359 --> 00:48:17,663
It turns out this Anointed One was cut off,

851
00:48:18,175 --> 00:48:19,199
having nothing —

852
00:48:20,991 --> 00:48:22,015
not for Himself.

853
00:48:23,807 --> 00:48:24,575
He is the One who

854
00:48:24,831 --> 00:48:26,111
loved me and gave Himself for me.

855
00:48:30,463 --> 00:48:34,303
It turns out that God used a method like this to save you and me.

856
00:48:35,840 --> 00:48:38,911
The Bible says it like this: when we,

857
00:48:38,960 --> 00:48:40,703
like sheep, had gone astray,

858
00:48:41,727 --> 00:48:43,007
each one turning to his own way,

859
00:48:43,007 --> 00:48:46,335
it says that the LORD —

860
00:48:46,335 --> 00:48:47,103
that is, the Father —

861
00:48:47,120 --> 00:48:50,943
would lay the iniquity of us all upon Him,

862
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:53,503
upon the Son, the Lord Jesus.

863
00:48:53,503 --> 00:48:58,480
This is what Isaiah chapter 53 goes on to say.

864
00:48:59,647 --> 00:49:02,463
God used this method, the method of substitution.

865
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:05,023
He died for us

866
00:49:05,535 --> 00:49:06,559
so that today we

867
00:49:06,815 --> 00:49:07,583
could

868
00:49:07,583 --> 00:49:10,143
have our sins forgiven.

869
00:49:10,143 --> 00:49:13,215
He died for us so that today we could have life.

870
00:49:16,031 --> 00:49:17,823
So the Chinese character for "righteousness" —

871
00:49:18,335 --> 00:49:19,871
how is it written? It is a lamb

872
00:49:20,639 --> 00:49:21,407
placed over "me."

873
00:49:22,687 --> 00:49:24,991
It turns out the Lord Jesus died in my place.

874
00:49:25,759 --> 00:49:27,551
He is the Passover lamb.

875
00:49:29,343 --> 00:49:32,671
And when He died in my place, for me, today I can be justified.

876
00:49:32,671 --> 00:49:35,997
My sin is fully dealt with; I have sin no more.

877
00:49:36,255 --> 00:49:38,047
And I am able to know

878
00:49:38,303 --> 00:49:39,583
and enjoy a free, abundant life,

879
00:49:40,095 --> 00:49:40,863
to know

880
00:49:41,119 --> 00:49:42,655
what is beautiful and what is good.

881
00:49:46,239 --> 00:49:49,823
How precious — after the Lord died, on the third day He rose again from the dead.

882
00:49:49,823 --> 00:49:52,895
In fact, that year was very special,

883
00:49:52,895 --> 00:49:54,175
because that year the

884
00:49:54,687 --> 00:49:55,455
Passover

885
00:49:55,711 --> 00:49:57,247
fell on a Friday.

886
00:49:58,271 --> 00:50:01,343
So after the Lord died, next came

887
00:50:01,855 --> 00:50:06,719
the Feast of Unleavened Bread — and in fact the Feast of Unleavened Bread means that the effect of the Lord's death was immediate.

888
00:50:06,975 --> 00:50:08,511
That is, He dealt with our sin.

889
00:50:10,303 --> 00:50:13,119
Then, after the Sabbath, after Saturday,

890
00:50:13,375 --> 00:50:14,399
on the third day,

891
00:50:14,399 --> 00:50:17,680
the first day of the week, the Lord rose again,

892
00:50:17,680 --> 00:50:20,386
fulfilling the Lord's own word that He would rise again after three days.

893
00:50:20,386 --> 00:50:21,311
Do you remember we said

894
00:50:21,311 --> 00:50:24,383
that the Feast of Firstfruits is not necessarily three days afterward?

895
00:50:24,383 --> 00:50:26,383
But that year was so special:

896
00:50:28,991 --> 00:50:32,319
the Feast of Firstfruits, the third day after the Passover.

897
00:50:32,831 --> 00:50:37,439
The Feast of Firstfruits shows that the Lord Jesus is the firstfruits.

898
00:50:37,439 --> 00:50:39,695
He was the first to rise from the dead for us.

899
00:50:39,695 --> 00:50:44,080
And the Bible also says that just as He rose, so one day we too shall rise.

900
00:50:44,080 --> 00:50:46,143
The Lord's resurrection declares one thing:

901
00:50:46,143 --> 00:50:48,191
that He has already dealt with our sin.

902
00:50:48,191 --> 00:50:52,033
For if He had not dealt with it, He could not have risen,

903
00:50:53,311 --> 00:50:55,615
because the wages of sin is death.

904
00:50:55,615 --> 00:51:00,066
But the Lord's resurrection lets us know that this salvation has already been accomplished.

905
00:51:02,271 --> 00:51:02,783
Today,

906
00:51:03,039 --> 00:51:04,063
anyone at all,

907
00:51:04,575 --> 00:51:07,135
as long as he is willing to receive the Lord Jesus as his Savior —

908
00:51:07,391 --> 00:51:09,695
the Lord is able to help him

909
00:51:10,207 --> 00:51:11,231
overcome sin.

910
00:51:12,255 --> 00:51:13,535
Is that not "to finish the transgression"?

911
00:51:13,535 --> 00:51:16,962
He is also able to forgive the sins of a whole lifetime.

912
00:51:17,119 --> 00:51:18,399
Is that not "to make reconciliation for iniquity"?

913
00:51:18,911 --> 00:51:20,959
He will do away with our sin.

914
00:51:20,959 --> 00:51:24,470
The Lord came for this very purpose.

915
00:51:25,567 --> 00:51:27,615
And once sin is dealt with, there is no more

916
00:51:27,871 --> 00:51:30,687
wall of sin to separate us.

917
00:51:31,199 --> 00:51:33,503
Do you see the pair of hands that God stretches out?

918
00:51:34,271 --> 00:51:36,319
He wants to gather us into His embrace.

919
00:51:36,575 --> 00:51:38,111
We can cast ourselves

920
00:51:38,367 --> 00:51:43,231
into the welcoming arms of God, into the loving

921
00:51:43,487 --> 00:51:44,255
embrace of God.

922
00:51:46,815 --> 00:51:49,631
And God gives us the richest and very best preparation,

923
00:51:49,887 --> 00:51:52,959
so that we can receive every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places.

924
00:51:52,959 --> 00:51:54,751
Our sins are forgiven,

925
00:51:54,751 --> 00:51:58,079
and we can have true love, and true peace and joy.

926
00:51:58,079 --> 00:52:01,122
We are reconciled to God, shaking hands and making peace,

927
00:52:01,122 --> 00:52:03,989
beginning an abundant life,

928
00:52:05,503 --> 00:52:09,599
able to become the children of God, with a bright and warm home in heaven.

929
00:52:11,391 --> 00:52:11,903
And one day,

930
00:52:12,159 --> 00:52:14,719
the Lord will come again to take us there to Himself.

931
00:52:15,231 --> 00:52:16,255
Where He is,

932
00:52:16,511 --> 00:52:17,791
there we too shall be.

933
00:52:18,303 --> 00:52:20,863
So you see that the Lord is the bright morning star.

934
00:52:23,679 --> 00:52:25,727
And having come to this point, I would like to take a little time

935
00:52:26,239 --> 00:52:29,567
for any friend here at our gathering today who, if you do not yet know,

936
00:52:30,335 --> 00:52:32,127
if you have not yet received the Lord Jesus as your Savior —

937
00:52:32,639 --> 00:52:33,919
you can make this decision.

938
00:52:34,687 --> 00:52:35,967
You can pray to the Lord Jesus.

939
00:52:36,991 --> 00:52:38,527
You may pray in your heart,

940
00:52:39,039 --> 00:52:41,855
or you may pray softly aloud —

941
00:52:42,111 --> 00:52:43,135
and the meaning is this:

942
00:52:43,391 --> 00:52:44,159
Lord Jesus,

943
00:52:44,927 --> 00:52:46,207
I am willing to repent,

944
00:52:46,719 --> 00:52:47,487
and to sin no more.

945
00:52:48,511 --> 00:52:50,559
I ask You to forgive all the sins of my whole life.

946
00:52:51,839 --> 00:52:54,399
I am willing to receive You as my own personal Savior.

947
00:52:55,935 --> 00:52:56,959
A sincere prayer.

948
00:52:58,751 --> 00:53:01,567
And when you pray like this, God is deeply responsive.

949
00:53:03,359 --> 00:53:04,639
When Daniel prayed,

950
00:53:05,151 --> 00:53:06,687
God gave him the seventy sevens.

951
00:53:07,711 --> 00:53:09,503
God is deeply responsive, and when you

952
00:53:09,759 --> 00:53:16,880
pray to the Lord in true sincerity like this — the Lord came to bear your sin, and to forgive your sin.

953
00:53:16,880 --> 00:53:20,355
He died upon the cross for this very purpose.

954
00:53:21,279 --> 00:53:24,607
He will surely forgive your sin, and cleanse you from all unrighteousness.

955
00:53:26,399 --> 00:53:27,679
Let us take a little time

956
00:53:28,703 --> 00:53:29,215
for any friend here today

957
00:53:29,983 --> 00:53:33,055
who has not yet received the Lord, to make this decision.

958
00:53:35,103 --> 00:53:37,919
If you are willing to receive the Lord as your Savior,

959
00:53:38,687 --> 00:53:40,735
you can pray with me like this.

960
00:53:40,991 --> 00:53:41,759
I'll say a line,

961
00:53:42,271 --> 00:53:43,039
and you say a line after me;

962
00:53:43,295 --> 00:53:44,831
or you may simply pray in your heart.

963
00:53:47,135 --> 00:53:47,903
Do not hesitate.

964
00:53:48,415 --> 00:53:50,207
The people around you long for you to believe in the Lord.

965
00:53:50,719 --> 00:53:52,511
God has prepared this salvation for you.

966
00:53:53,023 --> 00:53:55,327
If today you are willing to receive the Lord as

967
00:53:55,583 --> 00:53:56,607
your Savior,

968
00:53:56,863 --> 00:53:57,887
you can pray like this.

969
00:53:58,143 --> 00:53:58,911
Let us begin.

970
00:54:00,959 --> 00:54:01,727
Lord Jesus,

971
00:54:03,775 --> 00:54:04,799
I am willing to repent,

972
00:54:05,823 --> 00:54:06,847
and to sin no more.

973
00:54:09,151 --> 00:54:11,199
I ask You to forgive all the sins of my whole life.

974
00:54:13,503 --> 00:54:14,783
I am willing to receive You as my own personal Savior.

975
00:54:18,111 --> 00:54:19,135
A sincere prayer.

976
00:54:23,231 --> 00:54:26,303
If you prayed along just now with that prayer, congratulations to you.

977
00:54:26,559 --> 00:54:32,703
And you can tell the friend who invited you to our gathering today, "I have come to believe in the Lord."

978
00:54:34,239 --> 00:54:35,775
In fact, the Feasts of the LORD

979
00:54:36,543 --> 00:54:38,847
could be called God's own calendar.

980
00:54:40,127 --> 00:54:41,151
At the Lord's first coming,

981
00:54:43,199 --> 00:54:44,479
He was the Passover lamb.

982
00:54:45,503 --> 00:54:46,783
He dealt with our sin.

983
00:54:47,295 --> 00:54:49,087
Then came the Feast of Unleavened Bread —

984
00:54:49,343 --> 00:54:53,120
His salvation is powerful and complete.

985
00:54:53,120 --> 00:54:54,833
And He rose again for us.

986
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:56,135
How precious — then the Holy Spirit came, and the family of God appeared.

987
00:54:59,327 --> 00:55:03,167
Just as the Lord, at His first coming, fulfilled the words of the Bible,

988
00:55:03,679 --> 00:55:06,239
in the same way you'll find that the Lord Jesus will come a second time.

989
00:55:06,239 --> 00:55:10,443
He will come back to receive all who believe in Him, to take them to Himself,

990
00:55:10,847 --> 00:55:14,943
and He has, for us, prepared a glorious eternity.

991
00:55:19,295 --> 00:55:20,831
May the days ahead of you

992
00:55:21,599 --> 00:55:24,927
bring an ever-deeper experience of the Lord, and may the Lord's love be with you always.
